From 286dd329826edb368d5070688c1fed20e9e90176 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mika Tammi <mikatammi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 14:26:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] rts: include <wasi/api.h> in wasm JSFFI.c

JSFFI.c calls __wasi_args_sizes_get()/__wasi_args_get() and uses
__wasi_errno_t, but relied on <wasi/api.h> being included transitively by
other libc headers. Newer wasi-libc (e.g. wasi-sdk 32) moved the preview 1
API to <wasi/wasip1.h>, which <wasi/api.h> includes for __wasip1__, and no
longer pulls it into the common headers, so building the RTS fails with

    rts/wasm/JSFFI.c:100:3: error: use of undeclared identifier '__wasi_errno_t'

Include the header explicitly.

Assisted-by: Claude Code (claude-opus-5-5)
---
 rts/wasm/JSFFI.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/rts/wasm/JSFFI.c b/rts/wasm/JSFFI.c
index 69f9fd0..45f1226 100644
--- a/rts/wasm/JSFFI.c
+++ b/rts/wasm/JSFFI.c
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 #include "sm/Sanity.h"
 
 #include <sysexits.h>
+#include <wasi/api.h>
 
 #if defined(__wasm_reference_types__)
 
